revision.text:
[[File:Kyotoreizangokoku haiden.jpg|thumb|The Kyoto Gokoku Shrine.]]
The '''Gokoku Shrine''' (Japanese: 京都霊山護国神社
) is a Shinto Shrine of the city of [[Kyoto]], [[Japan]]. It honors the heroes of Japan, especially from the period of the [[Bakumatsu]] period and the [[Meiji Restoration]].<ref name="Martin 65">[http://books.google.com/books?id=YRCWtf_d5jgC&pg=PA65 ''Kyoto Cultural Guide'' by John H. Martin, Phyllis G. Martin p.65]</ref>

The Museum is next to the [[Ryozen Historical Museum]].<ref name="Martin 65"/>

==See also==
* [[List of Shinto shrines in Japan]]

==Notes==
{{reflist}}

[[Category:Kyoto]]

{{jp:京都霊山護国神社}}

[[File:Kyoto Ryozen Gokoku Shrine01-r.jpg|thumb|upright=2|Kyoto Ryozen Gokoku Shrine]]
{{multiple image| align = right | direction = horizontal | header = | header_align = left/right/center | footer = '''Left image''': Tomb of Sakamoto Ryōma, in ''Kyoto Ryozen Gokoku Shrine'', [[Kyoto]].<br>'''Right image''': Tomb of [[Sakamoto Ryōma]] (detail).| footer_align = left | image1 =Tomb of Sakamoto Ryoma torii.jpg| width1 = 137 | caption1  = | image2 =Tomb of Sakamoto Ryoma center.jpg| width2 = 263 | caption2 = }}
The {{nihongo|'''Kyoto Ryozen Gokoku Shrine''' | 京都霊山護国神社|Kyōto Ryōzen Gokoku Jinja}} is a Shinto Shrine located in [[Kyoto]], [[Japan]]. It honors the heroes of Japan, especially from the period of the [[Bakumatsu]] period and the [[Meiji Restoration]].<ref name="Martin 65">[http://books.google.com/books?id=YRCWtf_d5jgC&pg=PA65 ''Kyoto Cultural Guide'' by John H. Martin, Phyllis G. Martin p.65]</ref>

The [[Ryozen Museum of History]] is next to this shrine.<ref name="Martin 65"/>

